            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a local person, then the Telugu for a stranger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చౌరస్తా",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చౌరస్తా — caurastā — \"a town square; a crossroads\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చౌరస్తాలో పెద్ద గడియారం ఉంది. caurastālō pedda gaḍiyāraṁ undi. There is a big clock in the town square."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where four roads meet; the busy centre of a small town."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చౌరస్తా (caurastā) is usually traced to Persian chahār, \"four\", and rāsta, \"a road\", which came into Telugu through Hindustani: the place where four roads meet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
